(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[13 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [14 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [15 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [16 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [17 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [18 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [19 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [20 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [21 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [23 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [25 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [26 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [27 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [30 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [32 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [33 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [34 21 "// the work due at its death"] [35 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [38 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [45 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [48 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [49 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [51 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [54 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [57 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [60 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [65 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [66 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [75 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [90 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [101 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [127 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [172 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [185 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [199 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [210 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [211 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [231 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [232 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [253 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [260 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [261 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [278 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [279 1 "// tracked or queued; the number of dead objects handled."] [298 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [299 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [316 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[77 21] [81 27] [105 21] [165 29] [193 51] [205 42] [217 51] [226 24] [235 39] [236 64] [247 92] [255 25] [266 28] [266 55] [268 28] [282 16] [282 27] [305 51] [310 16]]} (go/file "finalize.go" :imports [


