;; Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 218"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's
;; death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a
;; class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its
;; address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval
;; breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference
;; counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found
;; unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields
;; the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with
;; a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared.


